# Lustra — smoke test data

## Why markers

Postman MCP, curl scripts, and Playwright create **real rows** in Postgres. Without markers, cleanup is unsafe. All smoke and e2e data must be identifiable by convention.

## Markers (required)

| Entity | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| User email | `{role}.smoke.{runId}@example.com` | `client.smoke.1723299840@example.com` |
| `runId` | Unix timestamp or CI run id | `date +%s`, `$GITHUB_RUN_ID` |
| Booking `Idempotency-Key` | `smoke:{runId}:…` | `smoke:1723299840:hold-1` |
| Master slug (e2e, later) | `smoke-{runId}-…` | when onboarding e2e lands |

- `role`: `client` \| `master` \| `admin`
- Domain **`@example.com` only** — never real domains in smoke
- Per-run fresh `runId` in scripts (see `apps/api/postman/run-auth-smoke.sh`)

## Cleanup (planned — not in auth PR)

Target: `packages/db/src/cleanup-smoke.ts` + `pnpm db:cleanup:smoke` in a follow-up PR.

| Flag | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `--dry-run` | default — print counts, no deletes |
| `--execute` | delete matching rows |
| `--run-id=<id>` | optional filter to one run |

Delete order (FK-safe): bookings/holds → refresh tokens → users (cascaded profiles).

Guards:

- Refuse `--execute` when `DATABASE_URL` looks like production
- Only rows matching markers above
- Log counts before delete

Until the script lands: reset local DB via `docker compose down -v` or manual `DELETE` by email pattern.

## Agents

- New smoke/e2e helpers **must** use these markers
- Do **not** add the cleanup script unless explicitly requested
